  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A Rotary Contour, Rotary Parallel or Rotary Offset whose path states the spindle C now has a first-traverse law on a mill-turn and on a lathe. Before this, no law judged that first rapid.\n- The post order is the lathe order. A C-stamped path carries `PARAM LiveTool`, and the engine refuses each post that does not declare `liveTooling` (`crates/post/src/post/engine.rs:243`). Only `fanuc-lathe.cps` declares it. Its `liveMove` writes `G00 C` with the turret at its index position, then `G00 X Z` to the first record. The mill post's Z-then-X/Y order is never posted for these paths.\n- New seam `crates/app/src/operation/rotary_traverse.rs`. It calls #3077's `verify::live_first_traverse` in the two rotary arms of `generate.rs`, after the C stamp.\n  - The stock, the parts and the turning steel (a chuck) are read in the part frame, at the angle of C.\n  - The fixed steel (a tailstock, a steady, the table) is read in the machine frame, on the +X station. This is the `verify::c_steel` convention (#486).\n  - The end and the start of the first move are judged. A hit is a refusal by name (`GenError::Invalid`).\n- `rotary_gate::c_center` is the one source of the spindle line, for the stamp and for the law.\n- A rotary kind on a mill-turn whose path states no C (a machine file with no axis lines) posts through the mill post. It now takes the mill laws (`mill_post_rotary` added to `mill_order`).\n- Op-stamp word `live-traverse-rotary-3096` for the rotary kinds on a lathe or a mill-turn setup. Those caches read Stale one time. No mill's stamp moves.\n- Premise (maintainer): the turret starts at its index position, the top of the travel. A program that starts low is not covered. The decision records this.\n\n## Fixture decisions (coordinator; the fixtures are tests only)\n\n- The shared C-axis bar fixture (box stock 14 x 14 x 34, top Z34; clearance 25; BN-0600) opened with a first record at r 2.000, Z28.000, inside the box stock. The posted `G00 X Z` went into uncut stock, and the new law refuses it. That is a true hazard.\n- `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_fixture`, `lathe_work_spindle`, `lathe_workholding_live` and `rotary_letter` now use clearance 40, as `c_axis_unwind` already did. Each test keeps what it pins.\n- `c_axis_unwind::a_rewind_through_stock_is_convicted_by_the_verifier` cannot keep its geometry on a mill-turn: the orbit and the first record are on the same clearance plane. It now asserts the mill-turn's refusal by name. Then it reads the verifier's `RapidInStock` orbit conviction on the same bench declared a mill, where #2965's swept law reports `FirstTraverseLow`.\n- Dropped: move the stock (more readings change); expect only the refusal (loses the verifier coverage); drop the override (changes the intent).\n- No shipped example, catalog project or golden holds a rotary kind on a lathe or a mill-turn. No shipped file changes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse_rotary_mill_turn::a_steady_on_the_station_line_refuses_the_rotary_contour_by_name`\n- `first_traverse_rotary_mill_turn::the_same_steady_opposite_the_station_stays_clear`\n- `operation::rotary_traverse::tests::the_stated_c_picks_the_lathe_order_and_no_c_the_mill_order` (lib)\n- `c_axis_unwind::a_rewind_through_stock_is_convicted_by_the_verifier` (both laws)\n\n## Readings (debug, on the final head unless noted)\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- On the final head: `c_axis_unwind` 7/7.\n- On the head before the last test change:\n  - `c_axis_live` 5/5, `c_axis_fixture` 2/2, `lathe_work_spindle` 5/5, `lathe_workholding_live` 3/3, `rotary_letter` 3/3.\n  - lib `rotary_traverse` / `first_traverse` / `rotary_gate` 12/12.\n- On the first head (before the fixture changes):\n  - `first_traverse_rotary_mill_turn` 2/2, `c_axis_live_world` 3/3.\n  - `drilling_cross` 9/9, `lathe_cross_drill` 9/9.\n  - `first_traverse_mill_turn` 3/3, `first_traverse_rotary` 3/3.\n  - `lathe_workholding_kinds` 10/10, `setup_align_mill_turn` 2/2, `setup_align_multiaxis` 10/10.\n- All changed blobs have 0 CR bytes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: not run, covered by the cut gate.\n- The full `camcraft-app` suite was not run. Only the binaries above ran.\n- The known limits of #3077 stay: the turret body is not modelled, the tool cross-section is read square, and the stated X/Z travel is not used.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3096-mill-turn-rotary-first-traverse.md`\n\nChangelog: A Rotary Contour, Parallel or Offset on the spindle C of a mill-turn or a lathe now refuses by name a first rapid from the turret's index position that passes the stock, a part or the steel.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #3096\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
